cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use base16384 web, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "base16384 web: a browser workbench for the base16384 text format"
abstract: >-
  A static web app that encodes and decodes the base16384 binary-to-text
  format in the browser, with file support in the reference tool's UTF-16BE
  format, a byte map, an alphabet browser, a client-side JSON API and a
  throughput benchmark running in a web worker.
authors:
  - name: "Aesthetic Vulpes"
    website: "https://github.com/didvc/"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/DecodeEncode/base16384-web"
url: "https://decodeencode.github.io/base16384-web/"
keywords:
  - base16384
  - binary-to-text encoding
  - web app
  - benchmark
references:
